      },
      "id": 1,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Vital signs",
      "type": "row",
      "description": "The six numbers that answer \"is it up?\". If they are all blank, the problem is not the app: it is the collection."
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "nora-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "How many prometheus.yml scrape targets are unreachable. Covers infra only (prometheus, otel-collector, caddy, cloudflared, loki, alloy, grafana) — api/worker/web/admin do NOT have a /metrics endpoint and therefore do not appear here.\n\nExpected: 0. If it stays at 1 permanently, suspect number one is the cloudflared job: in the current docker-compose.yml cloudflared is only on the `edge` network and prometheus only on `internal`, so there is no route. See the note on that job in prometheus.yml.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.5.1",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "nora-prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "count(up == 0) or vector(0)",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Prometheus Targets DOWN",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "nora-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "cloudflared_tunnel_ha_connections. cloudflared opens 4 outbound connections to the Cloudflare edge. Dropping to 0 is literally the 522 error that took nora.systems down — Cloudflare answers, but has no way to reach the origin.\n\ncloudflared's request counters (cloudflared_tunnel_total_requests) are NOT on this dashboard on purpose: they stay at zero over the QUIC transport and would give a false impression of zero traffic.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
